Here’s a C# example that shows how to publish events to Azure Event Grid using a custom topic, and how to handle those events using an Azure Function.


---

🧱 1. Setup Summary

You'll need:

An Azure Event Grid custom topic

An Azure Function as the subscriber (WebHook endpoint)

A C# client app to publish events



---

✅ Step 1: Create a Custom Topic in Azure

Use Azure Portal or CLI:

az eventgrid topic create \
  --name myCustomTopic \
  --resource-group myResourceGroup \
  --location westus2

Get the endpoint URL and access key:

az eventgrid topic show --name myCustomTopic --resource-group myResourceGroup
az eventgrid topic key list --name myCustomTopic --resource-group myResourceGroup


---

✅ Step 2: Publish Events from a C# Console App

using System;
using System.Net.Http;
using System.Net.Http.Headers;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Newtonsoft.Json;

class Program
{
    private const string topicEndpoint = "https://mycustomtopic.westus2-1.eventgrid.azure.net/api/events";
    private const string topicKey = "<your-topic-key>";

    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        var client = new HttpClient();
        client.DefaultRequestHeaders.Add("aeg-sas-key", topicKey);

        var eventPayload = new[]
        {
            new {
                id = Guid.NewGuid().ToString(),
                eventType = "MyApp.DataCreated",
                subject = "/myapp/objects/123",
                eventTime = DateTime.UtcNow,
                data = new {
                    message = "Hello from C# Event Publisher!"
                },
                dataVersion = "1.0"
            }
        };

        var content = new StringContent(JsonConvert.SerializeObject(eventPayload), Encoding.UTF8, "application/json");

        var response = await client.PostAsync(topicEndpoint, content);
        Console.WriteLine($"Status: {response.StatusCode}");
    }
}

> ✅ Install NuGet: Newtonsoft.Json




---

✅ Step 3: Handle Events in an Azure Function

This is an example Azure Function (v4, C#):

using Microsoft.Azure.Functions.Worker;
using Microsoft.Extensions.Logging;
using Azure.Messaging.EventGrid;
using System.Text.Json;

public class EventGridHandler
{
    private readonly ILogger _logger;

    public EventGridHandler(ILoggerFactory loggerFactory)
    {
        _logger = loggerFactory.CreateLogger<EventGridHandler>();
    }

    [Function("EventGridHandler")]
    public void Run([EventGridTrigger] EventGridEvent eventGridEvent)
    {
        _logger.LogInformation($"Event received: {eventGridEvent.EventType}");
        _logger.LogInformation($"Data: {eventGridEvent.Data.ToString()}");

        var data = JsonSerializer.Deserialize<JsonElement>(eventGridEvent.Data.ToString());
        _logger.LogInformation($"Message: {data.GetProperty("message").GetString()}");
    }
}

> 📦 Make sure to install the Azure.Messaging.EventGrid package.




---

🔗 Step 4: Subscribe Azure Function to Custom Topic

Use Azure CLI or Portal to create a subscription from the custom topic to the Azure Function URL.

az eventgrid event-subscription create \
  --name myFunctionSub \
  --source-resource-id /subscriptions/<sub-id>/resourceGroups/myResourceGroup/providers/Microsoft.EventGrid/topics/myCustomTopic \
  --endpoint https://<functionapp>.azurewebsites.net/runtime/webhooks/EventGrid?functionName=EventGridHandler


